# .dockerignore - Exclude files from Docker build context
# This significantly speeds up builds and reduces image size

# Node modules (will be installed in container)
#
# `**/` is required. Unlike .gitignore, Docker matches these patterns against
# the full path from the CONTEXT ROOT, so a bare `node_modules` excludes only
# the top-level one — services/contact-api/node_modules and
# services/fluxology-mcp/node_modules were both still being sent to the daemon
# and ingested by the builder stage's `COPY . .`.
**/node_modules
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# Build output (will be generated in container)
dist
.astro

# Git
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Environment files (use docker-compose env instead)
# Exclude ALL env files so real secrets never land in the image via `COPY . .`
# — at every depth, not just the top level. services/dashboard-api builds with
# `context: .` and has no .dockerignore of its own, so it inherits this file;
# a services/*/.env would otherwise be in its build context.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.env

# Runtime data written by the services when run locally. Every record in
# services/contact-api/data/inquiries.jsonl is real personal information.
**/data/*.jsonl
services/*/data

# IDE
.vscode
.idea
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
.DS_Store

# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Docker
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
.dockerignore

# Documentation (not needed in container)
README.md
README-ASTRO.md
ASTRO-MIGRATION.md
claude.md
docs

# Tests. `**/`-anchored (see the node_modules note above) and matching the
# naming this repo actually uses: every suite lives in a `test/` directory
# (singular) with `*.test.mjs` files. The previous patterns (`tests`,
# `*.test.js`) matched nothing, which is how the office-scout MCP test files
# ended up inside the published site image until 2026-08-17.
**/test
**/tests
**/__tests__
**/*.test.js
**/*.test.mjs
**/*.spec.js
coverage

# Operator-local tooling and agent working state: never needed in any image.
tools
data

# Credential material must never enter a build context (docker-compose.yml
# documents a ./secrets/ migration; mirror of the .gitignore entries).
secrets
**/secrets
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# CI/CD
.github
.gitlab-ci.yml
.travis.yml
.circleci

# Temporary files
tmp
temp
*.tmp
.cache

# Source maps (production doesn't need them)
*.map

# Package manager lock files (we use package-lock.json)
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Optional: Exclude source assets that are already optimized
# src/assets/raw

# Misc
.npmrc
.yarnrc
.editorconfig
.eslintrc*
.prettierrc*
# tsconfig.json is intentionally NOT excluded — the container runs
# `astro build`, which reads it.
